From 136b6e8e046c109096c4b4bdfadb324dd6b1995b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 05:18:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(properties): status from a 3-month window, with a
 WordPress override
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the RERA-number rule. A project's flag is now decided in this
order:

  1. status_override in WordPress — a person beats a formula. Auto falls
     through. This is the manual control that was asked for.
  2. Possession says delivered or ready to move -> READY TO MOVE. A
     statement of fact about a finished building; no date arithmetic
     should be able to contradict it.
  3. Within three months of the launch date -> PRE-LAUNCH. The launch
     date is the UP RERA project registration date, so a freshly
     registered project reads as pre-launch for its first quarter and
     moves on by itself, with nothing to remember.
  4. Otherwise -> UNDER CONSTRUCTION. Projects with no launch date land
     here deliberately: a missing date is not evidence of a new launch.

The RERA number no longer decides anything. It misfired: a blank number
can equally mean a project finished years ago and dropped off the
registered list, which was true of three delivered towers.

Property pages now show all three registration dates from UP RERA —
Proposed Start, RERA Completion, and the registration date itself as
Launch — via the new rera_start_date field.

Data written to WordPress alongside this: launch_date and rera_start_date
for 42 projects, taken from the registered-projects table. ACE Arte is
registration 2026-07-28, start 2026-08-15, completion 2031-02-15, exactly
as specified.
